    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d756">

                <pb facs="0656" n="644" xml:id="pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890E.01/123: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-20T23:00:00-04:00">February 20,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>25. Your no. 11, January 16, and no. 35, February 6, 9 p.m. The question of the
                    recognition of Syrian and Lebanese independence continues to receive the
                    Department’s very active consideration, and although there are certain
                    inter-related problems which complicate the question, a further instruction to
                    you should be possible in the near future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
